A(('h1', S9))
A(('bul', [
    '**Between accounts.** Matthew has “the wicked one,” Mark has “Satan,” and Luke has “the devil.” Mark has “The sower soweth the word”; Luke has “The seed is the word of God”; Matthew has “the word of the kingdom.” Each is kept in its own account.',
    '**Between characters.** The sower sows. The fowls devour. The one who hears the word is described in each place. Jesus does not name the sower, the fowls, the sun or the thorns by saying what they are.',
    '**Between actions.** The way-side seed is taken. The stony-ground seed springs up and withers. The thorn-ground seed is choked. The good-ground seed bears fruit. Each action stays with its place.',
    '**Between settings.** The story is told to the multitude and the questions are asked by the disciples. The “mysteries of the kingdom” given to the disciples are Kingdom matters and not the Mystery given to Paul.',
    '**Between this parable and its neighbors.** The soils belong to this parable. The enemy and the tares belong to the Wheat and the Weeds. The Growing Seed has no soils. The explanation of one parable is not the explanation of another.',
    '**What must not be assigned.** No identity for the sower, the fowls, the sun, the thorns or the three amounts of fruit. No identity for the Body of Christ among the soils.',
    '**What must not be made of the actions.** Hearing, receiving, keeping and bearing fruit are actions in a story. They are not steps by which a person is saved.',
]))

